//? Title: Samplesort: actual sampled splitters, buckets and fallback work
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Sort comparable keys by partitioning around several sampled splitters. Native
events expose the actual sample, eight bucket sizes and recursive work; the
original fifteen-key and seeded 8000-key experiments are retained.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For a range longer than sixteen, take 24 deterministic evenly spaced samples,
sort them and choose seven splitters at indices 3,6,...,21. Upper-bound
classification places ties above the splitter. Concatenate eight buckets and
recursively sort them. Every key belongs to exactly one bucket, and every key in
an earlier bucket is no larger than any key in a later bucket; recursive
sortedness therefore implies global sortedness. A whole-range bucket falls back
to counted standard sorting to avoid infinite recursion. A depth fallback bounds
the stack. Distribution quality affects work; deterministic sampling provides no
random-input balance guarantee. The small original fifteen-key example uses
insertion sort only.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/samplesort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/samplesort.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::samplesort_trace(std::vector<int>{9, 2, 5});
    std::print("Actual before `{}`, after `{}`, comparisons {}.\n",
               r.steps[0].before, r.steps[0].after, r.comparisons);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Input [9,2,5]");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, "Actual insertion leaf (3 <= 16)");
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual output {}", r.values));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/samplesort_tiny.svg");
}
```
