> API and interpretation

Trace partition after-states precede child sorting and are retained in preorder.
All comparisons in sample, classification and leaf work are counted.
Standard-library sort counts can differ between implementations. The legacy
in-place adapter offers the underlying key operations basic exception guarantee;
run and trace own their working copies.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Frazer and McKellar, Samplesort: A Sampling Approach to Minimal Storage Tree Sorting (1970); deterministic variant here|https://research.ibm.com/publications/samplesort-a-sampling-approach-to-minimal-storage-tree-sorting]

